stanzas:
Therefore we, before him bending, * This great Sacrament revere;
Types and shadows have their ending, * For the newer rite is here;
Faith, our outward sense befriending, * Makes our inward vision clear.

Glory let us give and blessing * To the Father and the Son,
Honour, thanks, and praise addressing, * While eternal ages run;
Ever too his love confessing * Who from One with Both is One. Amen.

stanzasLatin:
Genitóri, Genitóque, * Laus et jubilátio;
Sálus, hónor, vírtus quoque * Sit et benedíctio.
Procedénti ab unóque * Cómpar sit laudátio. Amen.
